WEBVTT

00:06.047 --> 00:08.049
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.066 --> 01:07.317
[inhales]

01:08.526 --> 01:09.903
[exhales]

01:09.986 --> 01:11.988
[mystical music playing]

01:13.865 --> 01:18.036
"Make sure you are
punished too, spirit." [laughs smugly]

01:19.329 --> 01:21.790
That was already 20 years ago.

01:21.873 --> 01:25.335
But no matter how long I wait,
the punishment just doesn't come.

01:25.418 --> 01:28.338
[Sade] You should still be careful.

01:28.421 --> 01:30.840
And watch what you say and do.

01:30.924 --> 01:31.883
Quiet, you.

01:32.717 --> 01:34.552
Why should I be careful?

01:34.636 --> 01:37.013
I am the almighty Genie, after all.

01:37.931 --> 01:40.016
[Sade] Man, this is stressful.

01:41.601 --> 01:42.811
[exhales]

01:45.605 --> 01:47.774
[whooshing]

01:53.696 --> 01:55.198
-[camel grunts]
-[Iblis] Huh?

02:00.120 --> 02:01.496
The smell of this clay.

02:01.579 --> 02:04.207
[dramatic music swells]

02:10.630 --> 02:12.257
[dramatic music ends]

02:14.425 --> 02:16.261
What the… You're that…

02:18.680 --> 02:19.556
You're still alive?

02:20.598 --> 02:22.767
-Who are you?
-Huh?

02:22.851 --> 02:25.687
How do you know the language of Goryeo?
Are you from Goryeo?

02:26.437 --> 02:27.772
Don't you remember me?

02:28.982 --> 02:29.816
[sniffs]

02:30.525 --> 02:33.570
It's definitely you.
You've been alive all this time?

02:34.154 --> 02:36.865
I clearly remember seeing you die.
Your breath just…

02:37.740 --> 02:38.992
I'm sure of it.

02:39.742 --> 02:40.743
[gasps softly]

02:40.827 --> 02:44.038
Seeing those bite marks, it is you.
Gee, you're a mess.

02:44.122 --> 02:45.248
You're being rude.

02:48.334 --> 02:50.420
I'm just really curious.

02:51.045 --> 02:52.130
I'm actually a genie.

02:53.131 --> 02:55.258
And we've met before. 20 years ago.

02:55.341 --> 02:57.635
Back then,
your final wish was my punishment.

02:57.719 --> 02:59.971
But I'm just fine. What do you think?

03:00.680 --> 03:01.973
Don't remember that either?

03:03.224 --> 03:05.810
[playful music playing]

03:05.894 --> 03:09.105
[in Arabic] Dates for sale!
Buy some dates!

03:09.772 --> 03:11.733
Dates for sale!

03:11.816 --> 03:13.276
[yelps, grunts]

03:16.362 --> 03:17.196
[gasps]

03:18.323 --> 03:19.198
[in Korean] Oh, no.

03:19.282 --> 03:21.784
[whimpers] My dates.

03:23.202 --> 03:24.787
[crushes]

03:26.205 --> 03:27.081
[Ka-young] Oh, dear.

03:27.165 --> 03:28.583
You're bleeding.

03:28.666 --> 03:30.710
You're more hurt than those dates.

03:32.045 --> 03:33.379
What a thing to say!

03:34.505 --> 03:36.007
You tripped me, didn't you?

03:36.507 --> 03:39.135
What are you going to do about these?

03:44.182 --> 03:46.226
What shall I do about this?

03:49.604 --> 03:51.898
Do I fully corrupt her,
seeing as she's survived?

03:51.981 --> 03:53.858
Oh, my, what a waste.

03:57.654 --> 03:59.864
I asked what you're going to do
about all these.

04:02.659 --> 04:05.245
-[playful music continues]
-[whooshing]

04:08.122 --> 04:11.459
-[gasps]
-How about this? Payment for the dates.

04:19.550 --> 04:21.177
[laughs]

04:29.435 --> 04:31.521
These are on the house.

04:32.522 --> 04:33.648
I hope you enjoy them.

04:35.650 --> 04:36.651
[in Arabic] Dates for sale!

04:38.069 --> 04:39.320
Buy some dates!

04:39.404 --> 04:42.490
[in Korean] Just look at you.
You're well on your way to corruption.

04:42.991 --> 04:46.411
You're already corrupt.
Great, let's just push a little harder.

04:47.078 --> 04:50.456
[in Arabic] Dates for sale!
Buy some dates!

04:50.540 --> 04:53.251
[in Korean] I'm already having
so much fun. Where do you live?

04:53.918 --> 04:55.086
[in Arabic] Where is my money?

04:55.962 --> 04:57.046
My money's gone!

05:02.302 --> 05:03.761
[indistinct chatter]

05:05.096 --> 05:06.264
[in Arabic] Take this.

05:06.931 --> 05:08.057
Eat this.

05:14.397 --> 05:18.609
I got very lucky today.

05:19.652 --> 05:20.778
Please eat.

05:22.113 --> 05:23.031
[in Arabic] Thank you.

05:30.038 --> 05:31.581
[Ka-young, in Korean] Be careful.

05:31.664 --> 05:34.876
[in Arabic] Don't touch me,
you filthy slave girl.

05:34.959 --> 05:37.462
[somber music playing]

05:41.382 --> 05:43.426
[in Korean] I can't hear
any of those words.

05:45.011 --> 05:46.345
It's all so difficult.

05:47.847 --> 05:49.891
[sighs] I can't understand a word.

06:19.629 --> 06:20.546
My goodness!

06:21.464 --> 06:23.382
-[gasps]
-Hmm.

06:24.759 --> 06:25.593
You live here?

06:27.470 --> 06:29.263
How did you find your way here?

06:29.347 --> 06:32.100
Go away. I'll get cast out if anyone sees.

06:32.183 --> 06:34.102
Don't worry. Only you can see me.

06:35.812 --> 06:38.439
Besides, no one
seems to care about you at all.

06:39.482 --> 06:41.442
[indistinct chatter]

06:43.611 --> 06:45.488
[Iblis] Humans sure are shallow,
aren't they?

06:45.571 --> 06:49.617
They'll ostracize and judge you even
if you're just a tad bit different. [tuts]

06:49.700 --> 06:50.785
Don't bad-mouth them.

06:51.410 --> 06:54.038
They gave me work to do
and a place to sleep.

06:54.622 --> 06:57.583
[sighs] Just hurry and get out of here
before you get caught.

06:58.084 --> 06:59.293
I'm just intrigued.

06:59.377 --> 07:02.421
A human who used
all her wishes for others.

07:02.505 --> 07:07.343
One who even dared
to mention me in her final wish. Huh?

07:09.929 --> 07:11.013
Wow.

07:11.639 --> 07:13.641
That's what my punishment was!

07:13.724 --> 07:16.644
With no humans to corrupt for 20 years,
I almost died of boredom.

07:16.727 --> 07:18.312
That was my punishment!

07:18.396 --> 07:20.273
You lived, so I never found a new master!

07:20.356 --> 07:21.649
What are you talking about?

07:22.233 --> 07:23.776
I told you I've never made wishes.

07:23.860 --> 07:26.529
[scoffs] Well, well, playing dumb, are we?

07:26.612 --> 07:29.323
You're in this foreign land
with that face of a foreigner.

07:29.407 --> 07:33.161
You may act resolute now, but you will
eventually show your true colors.

07:33.244 --> 07:35.204
Then you'll be corrupt in no time.

07:40.334 --> 07:43.004
Did you say only I can see you?

07:44.130 --> 07:45.047
Yes.

07:46.382 --> 07:47.800
It's one of my main magical…

07:50.261 --> 07:51.971
But why aren't you surprised?

07:52.513 --> 07:53.723
Most humans are.

07:55.516 --> 07:58.603
You said you're a ji-ne.
We have centipedes in Goryeo too.

07:59.729 --> 08:03.483
The elders said that a thousand-year-old
centipede could wield magic.

08:04.066 --> 08:06.110
I'm a genie, not a ji-ne.

08:08.821 --> 08:11.073
So why did you ask
if only you could see me?

08:13.242 --> 08:14.619
It just seems like a shame.

08:18.998 --> 08:22.251
You're so striking when you smile.

08:22.335 --> 08:24.879
[gentle music playing]

08:24.962 --> 08:25.963
[chuckles softly]

08:37.934 --> 08:39.185
[Iblis] "Striking"?

08:39.268 --> 08:41.729
That must be
the highest of compliments in Goryeo.

08:41.812 --> 08:43.814
[indistinct chatter]

08:47.860 --> 08:48.986
[camel grunts]

09:00.456 --> 09:01.999
Why did you come here?

09:02.667 --> 09:05.002
Why else would I come to a camel market?

09:05.670 --> 09:06.796
I'm here to buy a camel.

09:06.879 --> 09:08.297
Why are you buying a camel?

09:08.381 --> 09:09.674
So I can return

09:10.466 --> 09:11.300
to Goryeo.

09:14.679 --> 09:18.516
[in Arabic] Are you looking for a camel?
All the good ones are over there.

09:21.477 --> 09:23.104
[in Korean] Stay here and don't interfere.

09:27.233 --> 09:28.818
-[clangs]
-[Ka-young whimpers]

09:28.901 --> 09:31.112
-[coins jingle]
-[man grunting]

09:31.195 --> 09:35.157
-[Ka-young] No! My gold coins! No!
-[man grunting]

09:35.241 --> 09:37.076
-[grunts]
-[Ka-young yelps, grunts]

09:39.161 --> 09:40.621
-[groans]
-[men laugh]

09:40.705 --> 09:43.124
-[sobbing]
-[men grunting]

09:48.754 --> 09:49.630
[in Arabic] Stop!

09:53.384 --> 09:55.219
-[whooshing]
-[gasps]

09:56.304 --> 09:58.014
-[squelching]
-[gasps]

09:58.097 --> 09:59.473
[gasps]

09:59.557 --> 10:01.392
[intense music playing]

10:04.103 --> 10:05.730
-[squelching]
-[body thuds]

10:05.813 --> 10:07.398
[man 1, in Arabic]
It's Shaytan! The Devil!

10:07.481 --> 10:08.983
[man 2, in Arabic] It's Shaytan!

10:09.066 --> 10:10.610
[gasps]

10:11.402 --> 10:13.487
Ah…

10:14.280 --> 10:15.698
[music intensifies and fades]

10:17.908 --> 10:18.868
[in Korean] Here.

10:20.119 --> 10:24.290
[voice trembling] You… really are Shaytan.

10:26.959 --> 10:30.796
How could you kill a person? [crying]

10:32.381 --> 10:33.466
He took your coins.

10:34.508 --> 10:35.760
This only happened

10:36.886 --> 10:40.431
because I was being
too greedy in the first place.

10:41.265 --> 10:45.227
[sniffles] I was paid too much
for the dates.

10:46.395 --> 10:48.022
[crying]

10:49.815 --> 10:52.151
I never want to see you again.

10:53.778 --> 10:56.197
[Ka-young sniffles, cries]

11:05.581 --> 11:07.583
[whimsical music playing]

11:11.253 --> 11:13.172
[leaves rustling]

11:13.255 --> 11:16.342
[dance pop music playing]

11:17.635 --> 11:19.637
[grunting]

11:23.432 --> 11:26.185
-[Iblis sighs]
-[Arabic folk music playing]

11:27.812 --> 11:29.980
-[music stops]
-[Iblis] Huh? [groans]

11:31.732 --> 11:33.526
[whooshing]

11:36.904 --> 11:39.240
I returned the coins
to their original owner.

11:39.824 --> 11:42.034
And that jerk really did deserve to die.

11:42.535 --> 11:45.746
You weren't the only one he wronged.
I'm sure the other humans would be

11:46.747 --> 11:47.581
happy.

11:48.374 --> 11:49.208
Probably.

11:50.626 --> 11:54.338
Hey, what am I supposed to do
when that's how I am? I'm Shaytan.

11:57.883 --> 11:59.427
When will you be

12:00.219 --> 12:01.220
going to Goryeo?

12:03.264 --> 12:06.058
Perhaps it would be faster
to cross the Gobi Desert.

12:09.478 --> 12:10.479
Want me to take you?

12:18.320 --> 12:19.405
Do you

12:20.990 --> 12:21.824
know the way?

12:22.533 --> 12:23.492
Somewhat.

12:24.326 --> 12:25.911
I once blocked the path.

12:26.871 --> 12:28.706
I'll find out, so stop being mad.

12:28.789 --> 12:30.166
Really?

12:32.084 --> 12:35.880
Then I'll start saving for a camel again.

12:36.464 --> 12:40.468
Please show me the way. [chuckles softly]

12:40.551 --> 12:42.553
[gentle music playing]

12:44.263 --> 12:45.306
[chuckles]

12:56.192 --> 12:59.445
Why do you live like this anyway?
Doesn't it make you angry?

13:02.031 --> 13:03.616
I died and came back to life,

13:04.283 --> 13:05.701
though I don't remember it.

13:07.578 --> 13:10.623
I must have gained
the scars on my body then.

13:12.917 --> 13:16.545
There must be a reason
I was kept alive in this world.

13:18.088 --> 13:20.216
And so, I should live life to the fullest.

13:28.390 --> 13:30.392
[gentle music continues]

13:37.858 --> 13:40.152
[leaves rustling]

13:50.871 --> 13:51.956
[Iblis] How foolish.

13:52.039 --> 13:54.124
There's no such thing as the right wish.

13:54.875 --> 13:57.378
To gain something,
something else must be lost.

13:57.461 --> 14:00.339
For someone to live, another must die.

14:01.340 --> 14:04.260
-Sade!
-[growls]

14:05.594 --> 14:06.595
[screams]

14:11.225 --> 14:13.227
[gentle music continues]

14:25.698 --> 14:27.825
-[gentle music fades]
-[indistinct chatter]

14:45.092 --> 14:47.386
[coughing]

14:53.058 --> 14:53.893
[coughs]

14:59.940 --> 15:00.774
Khalid.

15:05.446 --> 15:08.824
[in Arabic] I bought this
from a Khitan merchant.

15:09.533 --> 15:13.078
He told me it was good for coughs.

15:13.162 --> 15:15.664
Boil it and drink the water.

15:18.542 --> 15:20.669
[in Korean] So you care
for all the young and old?

15:21.253 --> 15:22.129
Don't.

15:22.630 --> 15:25.591
Humans betray those closest to them
and never learn gratitude.

15:28.552 --> 15:30.095
[in Arabic] Isn't that right?

15:30.596 --> 15:33.974
I see you are half human and half spirit.

15:35.643 --> 15:37.269
[in Korean] Apparently, his father sings.

15:38.187 --> 15:39.563
[in Arabic] Are you Shadi's son?

15:40.773 --> 15:44.485
You are sick and weak
because you were born with a human body.

15:48.405 --> 15:50.199
[in Arabic] You're Iblis, aren't you?

15:50.824 --> 15:55.746
Are you not the leader of spirits?
Could you please make me better?

15:55.829 --> 15:57.748
Please make me a complete spirit.

15:58.332 --> 16:00.125
I know you can do anything.

16:07.091 --> 16:09.635
This thread can bind spirits.

16:09.718 --> 16:12.888
I will gladly
give this to you as an offering.

16:13.430 --> 16:14.598
I don't need it.

16:15.849 --> 16:20.312
We may be related,
but I simply cannot fulfill your request.

16:21.480 --> 16:22.398
[in Korean] Let's go.

16:24.274 --> 16:26.652
[suspenseful music playing]

16:55.097 --> 16:56.223
[whooshing]

16:56.306 --> 16:59.018
-[Iblis grunts]
-Aah! Aah…

16:59.643 --> 17:02.563
Hey, lie down to sleep.
Why are you sleeping like this?

17:04.064 --> 17:06.608
I told you to let me know
before showing up.

17:07.109 --> 17:10.946
Hey, how much clearer
could I have let you know… [chuckles]

17:12.197 --> 17:15.784
What are you making every night anyway?
While losing sleep too.

17:15.868 --> 17:17.119
Hanbok.

17:18.579 --> 17:20.330
To wear on my journey back to Goryeo.

17:22.666 --> 17:24.334
But I need to work during the day.

17:27.463 --> 17:29.089
It's dark as night in here.

17:30.215 --> 17:31.341
Follow me.

17:32.384 --> 17:34.386
[upbeat music playing]

17:43.270 --> 17:44.980
[Ka-young] This is where you live?

17:45.064 --> 17:48.025
Wow, it's like a palace.

17:48.525 --> 17:49.985
You've never been in a palace.

17:51.236 --> 17:54.198
Hey. I'm from Gaegyeong.

17:54.281 --> 17:57.284
There are so many
magnificent palaces there.

17:57.951 --> 18:01.497
Just standing at the gates
and seeing them from a distance, you know?

18:02.748 --> 18:04.958
Their presence is just, you know?

18:05.042 --> 18:06.710
So you've never been inside.

18:07.753 --> 18:10.255
I got close enough
to be practically inside.

18:10.339 --> 18:11.673
[Iblis] What else is there?

18:12.716 --> 18:15.511
-How does it differ from here?
-Mm…

18:19.056 --> 18:20.307
Goryeo has

18:21.058 --> 18:22.559
four distinct seasons.

18:24.019 --> 18:28.482
The summers are hot like it is here,
but in fall, the leaves change color.

18:29.900 --> 18:32.778
And in winter,
white snow falls from the sky.

18:35.072 --> 18:37.908
When the plum blossoms bloom
through those snowflakes,

18:39.201 --> 18:40.119
it's spring.

18:41.870 --> 18:45.082
And when the plum blossoms wither,

18:45.707 --> 18:49.545
the cherry blossoms bloom. [chuckles]

18:50.295 --> 18:54.007
-[chuckles]
-Cherry blossoms are really pretty.

19:01.723 --> 19:02.558
[chuckles]

19:04.935 --> 19:06.186
[chuckles]

19:10.190 --> 19:12.901
[romantic ballad playing]

19:22.953 --> 19:24.496
[Ka-young] Back in Goryeo,

19:24.580 --> 19:27.791
we wrote our wishes and sent them out
on boats down small streams.

19:28.458 --> 19:30.502
We believed
that the wishes would come true

19:31.378 --> 19:33.505
if the boat reached the ocean.

19:34.548 --> 19:38.385
Consider it the ocean at night.
How far shall I send them for you?

19:41.513 --> 19:42.764
Far, far away.

19:44.433 --> 19:47.227
Beyond the place
where the land meets the sky.

19:49.104 --> 19:50.230
Far away.

19:53.066 --> 19:54.401
All the way to Goryeo.

20:01.241 --> 20:03.785
[ballad continues]

20:07.289 --> 20:09.708
[Iblis] What did you write
on those boats anyway?

20:11.585 --> 20:12.836
[Ka-young] Never you mind.

20:15.505 --> 20:16.548
It looks like

20:17.549 --> 20:20.177
it's raining stars.

20:46.870 --> 20:49.456
PLEASE DO NOT LET THIS WANDERER STARVE

20:52.668 --> 20:55.837
PLEASE DO NOT LET ANYONE FALL VICTIM
TO THIS WANDERER'S STRIKING LOOKS

20:56.588 --> 21:01.510
PLEASE LET ME RETURN TO GORYEO

21:03.345 --> 21:04.763
[music fades]

21:04.846 --> 21:06.848
[all crying]

21:13.355 --> 21:16.024
[dramatic choral music playing]

21:23.240 --> 21:27.160
[in Arabic] It is Ejllael!
He has come to take my soul.

21:28.120 --> 21:32.165
[Ejllael, in Arabic] I will guide
your soul with these sacred wings.

21:32.749 --> 21:36.003
Did you say you will guide my soul

21:36.586 --> 21:39.298
with those sacred wings of yours?

21:39.381 --> 21:40.716
Your soul will…

21:40.799 --> 21:42.217
-[sharp snap]
-Ouch ouchy!

21:42.301 --> 21:45.304
-[music stops]
-[man] He says my soul will go ouch ouchy!

21:45.804 --> 21:47.556
[shouts] Ouch ouchy!

21:47.639 --> 21:49.516
[all wailing]

21:49.599 --> 21:51.977
[in Arabic] Hey,
you could just ask nicely!

21:52.060 --> 21:55.522
Why would you just pluck my feathers?

21:57.607 --> 21:59.234
[romantic waltz music playing]

22:01.069 --> 22:04.823
[Iblis, in Korean] You, who came
from Goryeo, were living as a slave.

22:04.906 --> 22:06.074
Serves you right.

22:07.617 --> 22:10.662
They say, in Goryeo,
there is a centipede that wields magic.

22:11.163 --> 22:13.957
I shall go up against it
when I get to Goryeo.

22:16.043 --> 22:17.753
You wish upon stars.

22:18.337 --> 22:19.629
[sighs]

22:22.215 --> 22:26.595
She used up all her wishes on others
and now makes wishes on silly stars.

22:27.596 --> 22:29.306
She even wished for my sake.

22:30.390 --> 22:35.062
To think that she is concerned
for my body and my meals.

22:43.737 --> 22:46.656
[Ejllael] Why should a fleeting moment
matter to one who is immortal?

22:47.157 --> 22:50.243
While Iblis was tied
to that girl's final wish…

22:52.245 --> 22:55.207
he was more interested in her
than in corrupting humans.

22:55.791 --> 22:57.918
Strangely, he seemed far more excited

22:58.001 --> 23:00.587
pondering what to feed her
and how to make her smile

23:00.670 --> 23:03.924
than when he was scheming how to corrupt

23:04.424 --> 23:05.884
another human soul.

23:06.718 --> 23:09.137
[tearfully] I know.

23:10.931 --> 23:12.432
[cries] It's just so sad, Master.

23:14.643 --> 23:18.271
-[continues crying]
-[sighs]

23:19.856 --> 23:23.610
I'm talking about how much
of a damn fool Iblis was.

23:23.693 --> 23:25.737
What am I to do
if you find this upsetting?

23:26.696 --> 23:28.865
I was too busy crying to see that, Master.

23:28.949 --> 23:31.660
-Would you please repeat yourself?
-[sighs]

23:33.537 --> 23:35.413
-Look carefully.
-[whimpers] Mm…

23:35.497 --> 23:36.748
Get out!

23:38.583 --> 23:39.835
[whimpers]

23:43.839 --> 23:44.965
[stifles sob]

23:52.055 --> 23:55.600
[sighs] Can't you find us some good clams?

23:56.518 --> 23:59.396
You keep bringing ones
full of these rocks.

23:59.479 --> 24:03.441
Eh. Just throw it out.
[exclaims, chuckles]

24:05.193 --> 24:06.486
[inhales sharply] That's hot.

24:08.738 --> 24:11.783
When will you complete that garment?
The Goryeo one.

24:11.867 --> 24:14.202
It's not easy to find the right fabric.

24:15.370 --> 24:18.331
-But I've almost finished.
-Can't you make it on the way?

24:19.958 --> 24:21.126
Let's leave after eating.

24:23.670 --> 24:26.506
Really? Can we really go now?

24:28.842 --> 24:31.678
-What about your lamp?
-Mm…

24:32.971 --> 24:35.849
I'll pray that he hurls it
with all his power to Goryeo.

24:38.268 --> 24:41.730
You who are singular and omnipotent.

24:42.439 --> 24:45.025
You are benevolent and noble.

24:45.901 --> 24:47.444
You are also merciful

24:47.944 --> 24:50.655
and wise, and, well…

24:50.739 --> 24:52.449
You're also…

24:52.532 --> 24:56.203
-You look incredibly desperate.
-[both laugh]

24:58.455 --> 25:01.082
[chiming]

25:03.585 --> 25:06.213
-Hey, you're…
-Mm?

25:07.088 --> 25:08.548
-You're glowing.
-Huh?

25:09.257 --> 25:11.134
It's a new master. But how?

25:14.471 --> 25:16.056
You were my last master,

25:17.015 --> 25:19.142
and I should still be tied
to your final wish.

25:20.018 --> 25:21.811
How is it I have a new master?

25:21.895 --> 25:24.231
I'm not quite sure,
but isn't this a good thing?

25:24.814 --> 25:28.485
You said you were really bored
with no new master in 20 years.

25:30.195 --> 25:31.321
Maybe you're right.

25:32.697 --> 25:34.699
Well, then, I'll quickly go
and corrupt them.

25:35.575 --> 25:38.370
[whooshing]

25:44.459 --> 25:48.338
-[breathing heavily]
-[whooshing]

25:53.593 --> 25:55.345
[ominous music playing]

25:58.598 --> 26:00.934
[in Arabic] We meet at last, Iblis.

26:01.017 --> 26:04.479
Because of you,
I have lived the past two decades

26:04.562 --> 26:07.649
as an oppressed foreigner.

26:13.571 --> 26:16.199
[music intensifies]

26:18.243 --> 26:19.953
-[grunts]
-Aah!

26:20.036 --> 26:21.246
[chimes]

26:22.831 --> 26:24.082
[whooshing]

26:24.165 --> 26:27.168
[man, in Arabic] It's Iblis! It's Shaytan!

26:27.252 --> 26:28.169
[rumbling]

26:28.753 --> 26:32.007
[in Middle Chinese] Where are you going?
Cast the Goryeo bitch aside too!

26:33.425 --> 26:34.843
-[man 1, in Arabic] Run!
-[man 2] Help!

26:34.926 --> 26:36.094
[whizzing]

26:39.723 --> 26:42.517
[Iblis, in Arabic]
So it seems I missed one.

26:52.861 --> 26:57.324
[in Arabic] I wish to possess more
than anyone born of this land.

26:59.993 --> 27:02.078
So my first wish

27:03.121 --> 27:06.249
is for you to make me
the richest person in the world.

27:13.715 --> 27:16.343
How predictable.

27:17.469 --> 27:20.388
Your wish has been fulfilled.

27:20.472 --> 27:22.599
[intense music playing]

27:23.308 --> 27:25.143
[panting]

27:44.829 --> 27:46.539
[indistinct chatter]

27:48.750 --> 27:52.087
-[whooshing]
-[sighs]

28:00.428 --> 28:01.262
You called me?

28:01.346 --> 28:04.641
I have decided on my second wish, Genie.

28:05.392 --> 28:09.396
Kill all those who looked down on me.
Let them die in agony.

28:12.399 --> 28:15.568
[in Korean] You really are Shaytan.

28:16.403 --> 28:18.613
How could you kill a person? [crying]

28:18.696 --> 28:20.990
[tense music playing]

28:25.370 --> 28:28.373
[in Arabic] Your wish has been fulfilled.

28:34.170 --> 28:36.089
[people crying]

28:39.843 --> 28:41.803
[woman wailing]

28:45.557 --> 28:46.683
[tense music fades]

28:46.766 --> 28:50.770
[Ka-young, in Arabic]
Dates for sale! Buy some dates!

28:51.271 --> 28:54.524
Dates for sale! Buy some dates!

28:55.900 --> 28:57.485
Dates for sale!

29:01.030 --> 29:03.575
-[sighs]
-[camel approaches]

29:08.788 --> 29:12.333
[tense music playing]

29:12.417 --> 29:16.713
[in Arabic] Uh, are you…

29:16.796 --> 29:20.842
I got very lucky today.

29:20.925 --> 29:22.135
Please eat.

29:22.761 --> 29:23.928
Thank you.

29:24.012 --> 29:27.348
[in Arabic] Yes, it is I.
Do you remember me?

29:27.849 --> 29:30.685
You gave me the sweetest of dates.

29:31.644 --> 29:33.605
Now I will give you everything you want.

29:33.688 --> 29:39.736
Garments and precious jewels.
A big house and countless servants.

29:39.819 --> 29:41.237
What do you say?

29:44.699 --> 29:46.701
I do not want anything

29:47.619 --> 29:49.788
I did not earn by my own effort.

29:50.413 --> 29:54.292
And I will soon be leaving
for my hometown.

29:54.375 --> 29:56.461
[laughs haughtily]

29:57.587 --> 30:00.089
[in Middle Chinese] You don't want it?
And you're leaving, you say?

30:00.173 --> 30:02.759
Now that I am looking down at you,
it is crystal clear.

30:02.842 --> 30:06.262
You are that slave girl
I bought to use as animal feed.

30:06.846 --> 30:09.933
And you dared to take pity on me?

30:11.935 --> 30:14.103
[inhales sharply, breath trembling]

30:17.065 --> 30:19.025
[Ka-young, in Korean] How does it look?

30:21.945 --> 30:24.989
Wow. It's beautiful.

30:25.073 --> 30:26.991
[chuckles softly]

30:27.075 --> 30:28.785
I had already finished making it.

30:29.786 --> 30:33.832
But I figured there was a chance
you couldn't leave this place.

30:34.833 --> 30:36.084
Because of the wishes.

30:37.085 --> 30:41.089
I don't know the way,
and I couldn't just leave you behind.

30:42.131 --> 30:44.676
-[chuckles softly]
-[chiming]

30:46.219 --> 30:49.597
Oh? It's Muttalib's final wish.

30:49.681 --> 30:51.724
[gasps] That means

30:52.308 --> 30:55.478
we really are leaving tonight, right?

30:56.187 --> 30:57.021
For Goryeo.

30:57.105 --> 30:59.065
Yes. Let's go.

31:00.066 --> 31:03.027
I shall go to see
the four seasons of Goryeo,

31:03.695 --> 31:05.864
where spring arrives
when winter snowflakes melt

31:06.531 --> 31:08.491
and the cherry and plum blossoms bloom.

31:09.075 --> 31:11.202
If you can't find me, just call my name.

31:13.079 --> 31:14.706
The name for you to call me

31:15.498 --> 31:16.666
is Iblis.

31:17.792 --> 31:19.127
Iblis.

31:21.462 --> 31:22.589
Is your surname "Lee"?

31:24.883 --> 31:25.884
Is that a good thing?

31:27.176 --> 31:29.804
-Let's say it is, then. [chuckles]
-[chuckles softly]

31:35.768 --> 31:38.521
-[gusting]
-[people exclaiming]

31:43.401 --> 31:45.445
-[people murmuring]
-[Iblis scoffs]

31:52.785 --> 31:55.955
[in Arabic] So let's hear it.
Your final wish.

31:56.039 --> 32:00.126
[in Arabic] After claiming revenge
and wealth beyond measure,

32:00.209 --> 32:05.590
I have found
that some things remain priceless.

32:05.673 --> 32:08.343
My last wish is her complete submission.

32:09.052 --> 32:12.805
Make that bitch stay by my side
for the rest of her life.

32:15.141 --> 32:17.393
[people exclaim]

32:22.315 --> 32:25.276
Your wish has been fulfilled.

32:27.195 --> 32:31.574
A heart that won't bow
for all the gold in the world?

32:31.658 --> 32:33.326
I'd like to see who this is.

32:33.409 --> 32:35.620
[suspenseful music playing]

32:49.133 --> 32:50.259
[in Korean] Why are you…

32:50.927 --> 32:53.221
[high-pitched chiming]

32:54.639 --> 32:55.765
Why are you here?

32:55.848 --> 32:57.976
[Muttalib, in Middle Chinese]
Why the hell are you here?

32:58.059 --> 33:01.229
I see. You have come crawling back!

33:01.729 --> 33:04.524
Of course, who could resist
all the world's riches?

33:05.024 --> 33:08.152
Bring her to me right now!

33:08.236 --> 33:09.821
[man yells]

33:09.904 --> 33:12.615
-[men grunting]
-[gasps]

33:13.241 --> 33:15.118
[screaming]

33:18.371 --> 33:19.998
[in Arabic] Why is Shaytan…

33:20.915 --> 33:22.000
[whimpers, shrieks]

33:22.750 --> 33:23.960
[both grunt]

33:25.086 --> 33:27.463
[in Arabic] Stop him! Stop Shaytan!

33:27.547 --> 33:29.340
-[pulsating]
-[grunts]

33:30.675 --> 33:34.429
-[tense music playing]
-[straining]

33:36.681 --> 33:40.435
[in Arabic] What is this thing?
Take it off! Take it off me right now!

33:43.646 --> 33:47.066
[screaming]

33:48.234 --> 33:51.779
[in Arabic] Since you refused my kindness,
I am proving my thread's worth.

33:53.197 --> 33:54.240
This is my thread's…

33:56.659 --> 33:57.535
use and power.

33:59.203 --> 34:02.540
[grunting, straining]

34:04.042 --> 34:08.379
-[whimpers, shrieks]
-[panting]

34:09.172 --> 34:11.132
-[pulsating]
-[grunts]

34:13.051 --> 34:15.636
[screaming]

34:16.637 --> 34:19.932
-[music intensifies]
-[continues screaming]

34:22.185 --> 34:24.228
[in Korean] Hunbish?

34:26.189 --> 34:29.776
-You're still alive?
-[Iblis panting]

34:30.985 --> 34:34.280
[in Arabic] So the boy who owned this body
was named Hunbish?

34:36.115 --> 34:38.076
[somber music playing]

34:40.995 --> 34:42.038
[Ka-young] Khalid.

34:45.500 --> 34:48.169
[gasps, in Korean] You're Khalid.

34:53.841 --> 34:54.926
How come you're…

34:55.426 --> 34:57.470
-How can this be?
-[people gasp]

34:58.763 --> 35:01.516
[Khalid, in Arabic]
Look! I've bound Shaytan!

35:02.141 --> 35:05.603
And this foreign girl loves another man.

35:05.686 --> 35:06.813
She loves Shaytan!

35:08.523 --> 35:09.524
[in Arabic] What?

35:09.607 --> 35:11.400
You didn't come for me.

35:11.484 --> 35:13.361
You came for him!

35:14.612 --> 35:17.698
[grunts] Get the bitch to her feet!

35:17.782 --> 35:20.326
[gasping, in Korean] Let go of me.

35:20.409 --> 35:23.871
Let go! [crying]

35:26.707 --> 35:30.294
[in Arabic] Make that bitch stay
by my side for the rest of her life.

35:33.297 --> 35:35.883
[in Korean] So this was
the wish that I granted.

35:36.884 --> 35:39.804
No. [straining, yelling]

35:39.887 --> 35:42.014
-[man yells]
-[grunts]

35:43.099 --> 35:44.809
I'm coming. I'll come to you.

35:44.892 --> 35:46.352
[whimpering]

35:46.435 --> 35:49.730
[in Arabic]
If I can't have her, no one can!

35:49.814 --> 35:51.482
[Iblis yells, grunts]

35:51.566 --> 35:53.943
[Ka-young shrieks, gasping]

35:54.485 --> 35:55.987
[screams]

35:56.737 --> 35:57.572
[in Korean] No!

35:59.824 --> 36:03.286
[haunting music playing]

36:03.369 --> 36:06.622
No! [gasps, yells]

36:06.706 --> 36:08.207
-[pulls out sword]
-[gags]

36:13.462 --> 36:15.965
[Iblis straining] I'm coming.

36:20.469 --> 36:22.388
No.

36:23.222 --> 36:24.515
Please, you can't.

36:28.311 --> 36:30.438
-[yells]
-[people gasp]

36:33.816 --> 36:38.779
[gasping] In Goryeo… [coughs, gags]

36:39.947 --> 36:40.907
No.

36:45.369 --> 36:48.164
Everyone has four lives.

36:51.834 --> 36:53.419
Whichever life it may be…

36:57.048 --> 37:00.009
come and visit me in one of them.

37:01.177 --> 37:03.971
No, please. Just hang in there. Wait.

37:04.555 --> 37:07.183
Just hold on. [breathing heavily]

37:13.272 --> 37:15.816
[in Arabic] I am Genie, the lamp spirit.

37:15.900 --> 37:19.862
I shall grant you three wishes.

37:19.946 --> 37:24.951
Please, I request any of you
to become my master

37:25.034 --> 37:30.831
and use one of your wishes
to save this girl.

37:32.792 --> 37:34.126
I beg you!

37:34.877 --> 37:38.839
Whatever it is you desire… [sniffles]

37:38.923 --> 37:43.344
…I will fulfill
your second and third wishes.

37:43.427 --> 37:45.388
[breath trembling]

37:45.471 --> 37:48.015
[chiming]

37:51.519 --> 37:54.146
[people murmuring]

37:57.191 --> 37:59.777
[people gasp, exclaim]

37:59.860 --> 38:01.445
[in Arabic] I will do it.

38:04.657 --> 38:07.118
Make me the richest man in the world.

38:07.201 --> 38:08.160
Richer than Muttalib!

38:08.244 --> 38:10.663
[gasps, in Korean] Please, no.

38:22.466 --> 38:24.760
[in Arabic] All right. Now, please.

38:25.303 --> 38:28.347
Before this girl takes her last breath…

38:30.349 --> 38:32.935
Please!

38:33.936 --> 38:36.939
It works. It really works!

38:37.023 --> 38:39.025
-But this is not enough.
-[Iblis, in Korean] No.

38:39.525 --> 38:42.153
[in Arabic] I want more gold. More!

38:42.236 --> 38:45.197
[sobbing, in Korean] No, this can't be.

38:53.998 --> 38:57.209
[in Arabic] Please.
This is your final wish.

38:57.710 --> 39:01.255
Please use your last wish
to save this girl.

39:01.339 --> 39:05.009
-[excited chatter]
-[tense music playing]

39:05.092 --> 39:07.928
[in Arabic] Please!

39:13.392 --> 39:15.603
[in Arabic] I want more gold, Genie.

39:15.686 --> 39:18.981
Fill this entire city with gold! [cackles]

39:20.107 --> 39:24.362
[in Korean] No, this can't be. Please.

39:24.445 --> 39:25.780
[in Arabic] We want gold too!

39:25.863 --> 39:27.323
Shower us with gold!

39:27.406 --> 39:29.450
[in Korean] This can't be. [sobbing]

39:37.458 --> 39:38.667
I'm sorry…

39:41.295 --> 39:44.090
for leaving you all alone.

39:44.173 --> 39:46.092
[sobbing]

39:50.137 --> 39:51.263
[exhales heavily]

39:59.355 --> 40:01.982
[sobbing] No!

40:02.066 --> 40:04.819
This can't be! No, please!

40:04.902 --> 40:06.362
Please, no!

40:07.655 --> 40:08.656
No!

40:23.087 --> 40:27.967
No, this can't be!

40:28.592 --> 40:30.803
This can't be. Bring her back!

40:30.886 --> 40:34.348
Bring her back now! Please! [sobbing]

40:43.941 --> 40:44.859
No!

41:16.765 --> 41:19.101
[tense music playing]

42:03.687 --> 42:04.855
[grunts]

42:12.905 --> 42:14.198
[Muttalib gagging]

42:20.996 --> 42:23.499
[melancholy music playing]

42:26.919 --> 42:29.505
[gasping softly]

43:01.036 --> 43:03.163
[people clamoring]

43:25.269 --> 43:27.313
[screams]

43:27.396 --> 43:29.315
[gusting]

43:29.398 --> 43:31.775
[screams]

43:31.859 --> 43:34.945
[dramatic music playing]

43:37.114 --> 43:39.825
-[screams]
-[rumbling]

43:45.914 --> 43:48.584
[people screaming]

43:50.961 --> 43:52.463
[laughing]

43:53.756 --> 43:54.673
[slashes]

44:14.193 --> 44:18.614
[Hunbish, in Mongolian]
Do you realize now how arrogant you were?

44:20.699 --> 44:21.950
[in Korean] At long last…

44:25.287 --> 44:26.705
that girl's

44:28.207 --> 44:29.541
final wish…

44:32.086 --> 44:33.212
was fulfilled.

44:34.463 --> 44:36.465
[gentle music playing]

44:39.343 --> 44:40.469
This…

44:44.598 --> 44:46.308
was my punishment.

44:48.102 --> 44:52.189
[in Mongolian] I was almost
sentenced to an eternal life,

44:52.272 --> 44:55.734
but thankfully,
faced death in another body.

44:56.568 --> 44:58.404
Then I became a wandering soul

44:59.279 --> 45:02.491
until I found you and my sister.

45:03.617 --> 45:07.037
Your punishment
has not yet come to an end,

45:07.121 --> 45:10.082
and you two are bound,
even in this life, by three wishes.

45:11.792 --> 45:13.794
[cries]

45:15.587 --> 45:16.547
[in Korean] That was…

45:19.007 --> 45:20.592
That was my doing yet again.

45:20.676 --> 45:27.057
[in Mongolian] And so, I return
this sad and beautiful story to you.

45:27.141 --> 45:30.644
Let your punishment for saving me be this.

45:31.979 --> 45:35.607
Whatever her final wish may be,
protect her,

45:35.691 --> 45:39.403
the one who was born to be wicked
yet still remains righteous.

45:46.618 --> 45:48.871
[in Korean] It is well overdue,
but I apologize.

45:49.371 --> 45:53.459
You were also one of the more
admirable humans that I've ever met.

45:54.585 --> 45:55.961
May your soul…

45:58.672 --> 46:00.090
find its way to peace.

46:16.023 --> 46:19.485
[breathes shakily]

46:24.740 --> 46:26.492
[sobbing]

46:37.419 --> 46:39.421
[melancholy music playing]

46:51.808 --> 46:54.520
[sobbing]

47:22.839 --> 47:26.468
[Iblis] Whatever the punishment,
I will take it.

47:28.428 --> 47:30.305
I will accept it willingly.

47:31.598 --> 47:32.766
I hope with all I have.

47:34.935 --> 47:38.397
Deliver whatever punishment
you see fit for my arrogance.

47:39.731 --> 47:41.275
I hope and plead.

47:42.276 --> 47:43.860
Of all I possess,

47:44.778 --> 47:47.573
take away anything
you see as more than I deserve.

47:49.324 --> 47:51.034
I hope against hope.

47:52.160 --> 47:53.287
Just once.

47:54.913 --> 47:56.290
Please, just once.

47:58.083 --> 48:00.294
Allow me to visit one of her lives.

48:02.296 --> 48:04.256
Deliver whatever punishment you must,

48:05.257 --> 48:07.175
and take away whatever you must.

48:09.011 --> 48:10.304
But just once…

48:12.264 --> 48:15.517
Please, just once,
in whichever of her lives…

48:19.521 --> 48:22.774
Whatever the punishment, I will take it.

48:24.776 --> 48:27.070
I will accept it willingly.

48:29.239 --> 48:34.745
Deliver whatever punishment
you see fit for my arrogance.

48:36.371 --> 48:38.081
Of all I possess…

48:47.674 --> 48:49.134
[gentle rumble]

48:51.303 --> 48:53.805
[twinkling]

49:02.814 --> 49:05.859
What are you saying? Pan-geum came where?

49:05.942 --> 49:07.444
She didn't come from anywhere.

49:07.527 --> 49:09.613
She never went to Hawaii
in the first place!

49:11.073 --> 49:12.991
Yes, is that you, Chang-sik?

49:13.075 --> 49:15.327
Hurry over to Pan-geum's house!

49:15.410 --> 49:18.538
-Just come when I tell you to!
-[groans]

49:19.414 --> 49:20.499
[Heung-rye] Follow me!

49:20.582 --> 49:22.542
-What is going on?
-Where are we going?

49:22.626 --> 49:25.629
[grandma] Oh, my! What happened?
What's all the fuss about?

49:29.841 --> 49:30.884
[sighs]

49:41.269 --> 49:42.729
-Welcome.
-[assistant] Welcome.

49:43.980 --> 49:44.815
Grand…

49:45.649 --> 49:47.776
-Mi-ju.
-[cries]

49:47.859 --> 49:50.696
-What is it? Why are you crying?
-[crying]

49:51.530 --> 49:52.823
Has something happened?

49:57.786 --> 50:01.581
My wisdom tooth just hurts so much.

50:12.551 --> 50:13.802
I'll take a look at her.

50:15.137 --> 50:16.221
[exhales]

50:17.806 --> 50:18.849
[sighs]

50:20.809 --> 50:21.643
[scoffs]

50:27.315 --> 50:29.818
-[pots crashing]
-[Heung-rye] You absolute witch!

50:29.901 --> 50:30.902
[Chang-sik] Mrs. Park.

50:30.986 --> 50:31.903
[Min-jae] Mrs. Park!

50:31.987 --> 50:33.989
Hey! Where have you run off to?

50:34.072 --> 50:36.032
Oh Pan-geum! Come out here right now!

50:36.116 --> 50:38.994
If you have nothing to hide,
come out this instant and say so!

50:39.703 --> 50:41.204
[Bok-ja] Heung-rye, please.

50:41.288 --> 50:42.664
[Chang-sik] Goodness me!

50:42.748 --> 50:45.083
What in the world
did you sacrifice to get that way?

50:45.167 --> 50:48.336
What in the world did you sacrifice
to get so young all on your own?

50:48.420 --> 50:49.629
-Come on.
-[Min-jae] Mrs. Park!

50:49.713 --> 50:51.673
Nobody's even home!
What's gotten into you?

50:51.757 --> 50:54.551
-[Heung-rye] Let go of me!
-Please just try to calm down!

50:54.634 --> 50:55.635
[Heung-rye] Let go of me!

50:55.719 --> 50:59.222
I'm telling you, Oh Pan-geum
must be using witchcraft or something

50:59.306 --> 51:01.516
because she's become
a young lady. You hear?

51:01.600 --> 51:04.853
Hey! I want to be young again too!
Me too, okay?

51:04.936 --> 51:07.105
-[Min-jae] No one's getting younger!
-Get out of there.

51:07.189 --> 51:09.399
-Let go of me!
-[Min-jae] You're not making any sense.

51:09.483 --> 51:12.194
Deacon An, just stay back.
Please, it's dangerous.

51:12.778 --> 51:15.280
Deacon? Is there even a god?

51:15.906 --> 51:20.327
If there is, there is no way
that he would let me become so miserable!

51:20.410 --> 51:23.580
My old age makes me miserable!

51:23.663 --> 51:27.292
Goodness me, I got so damn old
in the blink of an eye!

51:27.375 --> 51:30.921
-Lord have mercy! [wailing]
-[sighs]

51:32.172 --> 51:34.716
Right, this bitch. That's where she'll be.

51:34.800 --> 51:37.093
-The fields!
-[Min-jae] Where are you going now?

51:37.177 --> 51:39.012
[distant shouting]

51:41.056 --> 51:43.350
Oh. Don't get out.

51:44.309 --> 51:47.395
-I'll deal with the witch myself!
-[Min-jae] Chang-sik, please get up!

51:47.479 --> 51:49.022
She'll be in the onion field!

51:49.105 --> 51:50.816
[Chang-sik] You'll get yourself hurt!

51:50.899 --> 51:53.443
Calm down. Please calm down!

51:53.944 --> 51:58.031
Pan-geum is in Hawaii.
Why would she be in the onion field?

51:58.114 --> 51:59.115
[Heung-rye] Shut up!

51:59.199 --> 52:01.368
-[tires screech]
-[thudding]

52:01.451 --> 52:03.620
-[all gasp]
-[gasps]

52:03.703 --> 52:05.121
[gasps]

52:05.205 --> 52:08.458
[tense music playing]

52:11.920 --> 52:14.840
[breath trembling] Heung-rye.

52:15.340 --> 52:16.716
[gasps]

52:24.182 --> 52:26.226
[Bok-ja crying]

52:32.858 --> 52:35.861
You damn bastard! Get out!

52:36.736 --> 52:37.737
Get out of the car!

52:39.281 --> 52:40.574
-Get out!
-Get out!

52:40.657 --> 52:42.117
[Chang-sik] Get out of the car!

52:42.200 --> 52:43.869
[Jong-heon] What the hell
are you doing, punk?

52:43.952 --> 52:44.995
Get out--

52:46.580 --> 52:48.957
[tense music playing]

52:49.040 --> 52:50.292
Is this the police?

52:52.085 --> 52:53.378
I've just run someone over.

52:54.421 --> 52:57.382
Ishrun. You know what to do, right?

52:57.465 --> 52:59.301
I think she's dead.

53:00.093 --> 53:01.344
We're just outside

53:02.804 --> 53:04.431
Ms. Ki Ka-young's house.

53:04.514 --> 53:07.100
[tense music continues]

53:07.183 --> 53:08.727
[breath trembling]

53:17.027 --> 53:19.029
[rock fusion music plays]
